\[ S(0) = 1, \ S(1) = 1, \ S(k) = 2S(k-1) + S(k-2) \]

Given that definition, we can write a function that computes the nth NSW prime. We will need to generate the NSW sequence and check the rank of appearance of each prime in that sequence.

